    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2NrsjZR67sYLkLtKqkMhftf)_\n\n## What\n- `sp-search`: removed the `N` entry (`org-node-grep`) from the notes menu. `v` (`vulpea-grep`) and `n` (ripgrep) stay. Docs updated, including the stale `consult-notes` row that mentioned the Denote source.\n- `sp-graphs`: removed `(dg-use-denote nil)`. I checked the package source: `dg-use-denote` already defaults to `nil`, so nothing changes.\n- `sp-academic.org`: new section \"Removed citar packages\" linking the commits where `citar-denote` and `citar-org-node` can still be read, to salvage functions from.\n- Opened issue #319 about merging the citar packages' functionality into `citar-vulpea`.\n- `citar-org-node` itself was removed by #318; nothing more of citar is touched.\n\n## Testing\n- Docs tangle to the committed `.el` (ignoring whitespace). No test covers these menus.\n- /untested/ in the real Emacs.\n- No CHANGELOG edit.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9hnWskPJso94gsTkL)_",
